WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
2023 was the year that

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.920
artificial intelligence burst

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.839
into public consciousness,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.174
stoking the imaginations of many

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.510
and the fears of many others.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.847
In 2024, Goldman Sachs says generative

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:17.058
AI will move from an excitement phase

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:18.935
to a deployment phase.

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:20.603
And in the next ten years

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:25.567
could raise global GDP by as much as 7%.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.610
I was delighted to be able to sit down

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:28.695
with a fascinating

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.238
and brilliant entrepreneur

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:32.157
who has been at the forefront of

00:00:32.157 --> 00:00:34.200
AI for more than a decade.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.703
Mostafa Soliman was a co-founder

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:37.996
of DeepMind.

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:39.581
His most recent venture

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:40.665
is Inflection

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:43.543
AI, which he co-founded in 2022.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.086
What gets you interested

00:00:45.086 --> 00:00:46.546
in artificial intelligence?

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:46.921
Well,

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.590
I've always been obsessed

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.424
with the idea

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.468
that tools and invention

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:52.927
are going to make us

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:54.554
more capable as a species.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.097
And that's been the history

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.766
of human civilization.

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:59.225
We've invented things

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.643
in order to make our lives

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:03.646
easier and happier and healthier

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.023
and from a kind of

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.691
social impact perspective.

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:09.903
That's the grand offering of science.

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:10.445
You know,

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.739
if we look back over the centuries,

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.365
our lives have got radically,

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:15.366
radically better.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.535
And that's real cause to be optimistic.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:20.789
This engine of discovery and creation

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:21.915
is fundamental

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.457
to who we are

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:24.542
as a species of curiosity

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:27.879
drives us to create and do more with less

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:28.963
and that's

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:30.924
actually what drew me to

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.092
AI in the first place.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.426
So most people,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:33.968
I understand,

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:37.180
get the AI to do something specific.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:37.764
Let's say

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.140
look at a legal document

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.685
and find all the cases that relate to

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.271
or look at an x ray and figure out

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.273
compared to all the other x rays.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.819
Does this one have cancerous cells?

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:52.904
Help us understand generative

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:55.657
AI, which is the ability of the machine

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.909
to teach itself to think

00:01:57.909 --> 00:01:59.494
and then to go beyond that

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:01.538
to thinking kind of even more complex

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:02.664
and creative ways

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:04.874
than even human beings might be able to.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:05.625
So think about it

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.169
as two sides of the same A.I. coin.

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:09.879
For the last decade,

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:12.340
we've been focused on classification.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.716
How can we train deep

00:02:13.716 --> 00:02:15.468
neural networks to identify

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.470
patterns in data?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.305
And it's done that so well

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.057
that it can transcribe speech,

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:22.183
for example,

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:23.226
or it can understand

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:24.561
the content of images.

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:25.186
And that's been

00:02:25.186 --> 00:02:27.397
the classification revolution.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.440
The flip side of that is if the

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.733
AI now understands

00:02:30.733 --> 00:02:32.360
the difference between cats

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.487
and dogs and zebras in an image,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.030
you can then say

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.117
generate me a new example of a zebra

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.535
that's never been seen

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.953
with the color purple

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:44.956
and with bright blue wings, for example,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.875
because it understands those concepts

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:47.292
well enough

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.669
from having seen the historical patterns.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:50.587
Now, the third

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.755
phase of AI that's coming

00:02:52.755 --> 00:02:54.465
is interactive AI.

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:57.010
Now that you can have an AI generate

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.303
a new example,

00:02:58.303 --> 00:02:59.679
it can present that to a human

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.513
for feedback

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.514
and interact

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.516
in order to learn from the human

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.809
and be useful to you.

00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:07.270
Carry out new tasks In time.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.938
It will learn to use tools,

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:09.856
so it will actually be able

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.107
to make phone calls

00:03:11.107 --> 00:03:12.984
to other humans on your behalf.

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:15.069
Let me just get an example out

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:16.821
so people understand.

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:17.780
Correct me if I'm wrong,

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.866
but I think what you're saying is

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:23.161
you should be able to have an AI that you

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.455
say to your phone.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.041
Can you do the following for me?

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.000
Two weeks from now,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.627
I want to take a trip to London.

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:33.546
Can you get me a ticket, book me a hotel.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.632
I want to go to this restaurant,

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:37.050
make me the reservation.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.552
And I also need these three books.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.929
Can you order them?

00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:43.014
And the AI will then take it.

00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:45.433
Take care of it. All right. Exactly.

00:03:45.433 --> 00:03:47.435
Think of AIS in the future

00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:49.479
as personal assistants.

00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:50.438
Everybody is going to have

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.398
a conversational interface,

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.025
which not just represents you

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:56.319
and is there to help you and support you,

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.154
but can also teach you

00:03:58.154 --> 00:04:00.531
is actually going to help you day to day

00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:03.159
to be better at your job, to,

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.161
you know, make important life decisions

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:06.204
when you're thinking about whether

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.331
to relocate to a different city

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:09.457
or whether it might be time

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:11.000
to put your elderly parents

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.001
into a care home

00:04:12.001 --> 00:04:12.919
or whether to go ahead

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.129
and have a serious operation

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.005
that you're thinking about.

00:04:16.005 --> 00:04:18.007
So that gets to a very interesting point,

00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:20.051
which is emotional intelligence.

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:22.262
We've often thought that, you know, the

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.930
AI will do the analytic part,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.933
but human beings have this special thing,

00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:29.560
emotional intelligence, IQ,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.479
social skills.

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:33.273
You're saying the A.I.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.066
can have all that as well?

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:36.067
That's exactly right.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:36.484
I mean,

00:04:36.484 --> 00:04:37.652
we have developed

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:38.486
at my new company,

00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:40.780
Inflection, and I called Pie,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.032
which stands for Personal Intelligence.

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:45.451
And we've specifically conditioned it

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.495
to be good at emotional intelligence.

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:48.997
It's a great listener.

00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:50.665
It's very evenhanded.

00:04:50.665 --> 00:04:52.959
It presents both sides of an argument.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.003
It asks you great questions.

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:56.504
It tries to remember what you've said

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:57.588
in the past.

00:04:57.588 --> 00:04:58.965
It'll often paraphrase

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.841
what you've said in order

00:04:59.841 --> 00:05:01.426
to make you feel heard.

00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:02.427
So these

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:03.011
sort of

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:04.595
elements of empathy

00:05:04.595 --> 00:05:07.265
are actually quite learnable by the

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:09.267
AI and will be incredibly valuable

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.269
to millions and millions of people

00:05:11.269 --> 00:05:14.272
to have the comfort and support

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.482
of a friend, a companion,

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.234
an emotional intelligence in your pocket.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.569
I mean, I think people underrate

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:21.821
how significant that is in the world.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:22.530
Not all of us

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:26.993
have a supportive parent or husband

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.287
or wife or child or friend

00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:31.205
to help you get through difficult times.

00:05:31.205 --> 00:05:32.206
And now that it's going

00:05:32.206 --> 00:05:33.249
to be widely available

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:34.500
to hundreds of millions of people

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.710
over the next few years,

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.961
how do we stay in charge?

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:38.296
That's the key question.

00:05:38.296 --> 00:05:40.131
And I think in the limit, it's

00:05:40.131 --> 00:05:41.841
definitely possible

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.135
that we may not be in charge

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:46.346
and we have to confront that reality

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.513
that isn't desirable.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.265
It's not what we want.

00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:51.142
We don't want AIS

00:05:51.142 --> 00:05:53.144
that have autonomy in our world.

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:54.979
They shouldn't have rights,

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:56.689
as some people have proposed.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.484
We don't want new digital citizens

00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:01.611
hanging around in our everyday society.

00:06:01.611 --> 00:06:02.862
Just so that people understand

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.489
technically.

00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:07.367
Is it possible to say, Is it as simple

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:07.700
as saying,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.160
Look, at the end of the day,

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.579
you can always have a kill switch

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:14.332
and you can pull the plug?

00:06:14.332 --> 00:06:16.250
Or is it more complicated than that?

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.043
Yes, it's

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.628
going to be possible to do that,

00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:19.379
I believe,

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:20.755
if we focus on it

00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:22.673
as a research community,

00:06:22.673 --> 00:06:24.258
as a group of governing

00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:25.927
actors, as creators

00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:27.804
of the technology in the open source

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:29.263
and in the private companies,

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:30.765
we have to make that a priority.

00:06:30.765 --> 00:06:32.433
We have overcome

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:35.353
huge scientific and engineering feats

00:06:35.353 --> 00:06:37.271
to contain nuclear power,

00:06:37.271 --> 00:06:39.732
to get the best out of aviation

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.776
and not have planes fall out of the sky

00:06:41.776 --> 00:06:44.404
all the time to regulate cars

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.696
and make sure that everybody

00:06:45.696 --> 00:06:47.031
is trained to drive a car

00:06:47.031 --> 00:06:47.949
and that there are,

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:48.574
you know,

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.243
airbags and windscreens

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.912
and vehicle emissions and traffic lights.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:53.704
And, you know,

00:06:53.704 --> 00:06:55.456
these are important moments

00:06:55.456 --> 00:06:56.416
in the history of the development

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.166
of our technology

00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:58.918
where we've really paid attention.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.003
And this is another one of those moments.

00:07:01.003 --> 00:07:01.838
The good news

00:07:01.838 --> 00:07:04.841
is that over the last decade,

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:07.301
as the models have got bigger,

00:07:07.301 --> 00:07:10.179
they've actually got easier to control.

00:07:10.179 --> 00:07:12.014
There are fewer hallucinations

00:07:12.014 --> 00:07:13.433
than they have ever been.

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.892
There are fewer biases

00:07:14.892 --> 00:07:16.060
than they've ever been.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:16.894
And with each

00:07:16.894 --> 00:07:18.938
order of magnitude of computation

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.940
that we add to these training runs,

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:21.607
what we see

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.818
is that they make fewer mistakes,

00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:25.111
they're easier to control,

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.822
and they take instruction more closely.

00:07:27.822 --> 00:07:29.949
And so the real question becomes

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:33.119
whose instruction and what instruction?

00:07:33.202 --> 00:07:34.745
What is the behavior policy

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:35.746
that we're asking these

00:07:35.746 --> 00:07:37.415
guys to adhere to?

00:07:37.415 --> 00:07:40.376
And who is auditing and verifying

00:07:40.376 --> 00:07:40.835
that the

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:41.836
AIS are behaving

00:07:41.836 --> 00:07:43.087
within the boundary

00:07:43.087 --> 00:07:45.381
constraints that have been set for it?

00:07:45.381 --> 00:07:47.758
Tell me when when you look

00:07:47.758 --> 00:07:51.220
at the future of A.I.,

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:54.265
do you worry about something that

00:07:54.348 --> 00:07:55.475
Henry Kissinger and Eric

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:56.601
Schmidt have written a lot about,

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:57.351
which is that human

00:07:57.351 --> 00:07:58.936
beings will really be

00:07:58.936 --> 00:07:59.604
in a position

00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:03.107
of not understanding the world anymore,

00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:04.984
that before the Enlightenment

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:06.486
we didn't understand the world

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:07.695
and we would

00:08:07.695 --> 00:08:08.696
attribute anything

00:08:08.696 --> 00:08:11.532
we didn't understand to divine forces.

00:08:11.532 --> 00:08:13.576
You know, the sun rose was the sun.

00:08:13.576 --> 00:08:17.413
God moved his chariot across the sky.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.624
We will be in a situation where the

00:08:19.624 --> 00:08:22.168
the eye will tell us, you know,

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:24.086
this this, this is the answer.

00:08:24.086 --> 00:08:24.545
This is

00:08:24.545 --> 00:08:26.506
this person has canceled this book,

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:28.382
but we won't be able to understand why,

00:08:28.382 --> 00:08:30.551
because the level of computation

00:08:30.551 --> 00:08:33.554
and analysis will be so much greater.

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:35.932
What kind of position does that place

00:08:35.932 --> 00:08:36.891
human beings in where we are

00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:37.892
almost returning

00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:39.435
to a pre enlightenment self

00:08:39.435 --> 00:08:41.312
when the in that time

00:08:41.312 --> 00:08:44.315
we we looked up to a to God

00:08:44.315 --> 00:08:46.734
and now we look up to this black

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:47.735
box called the AI.

00:08:47.735 --> 00:08:50.321
But in both cases were believing

00:08:50.321 --> 00:08:52.240
not actually understanding.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.282
It's a great point

00:08:53.282 --> 00:08:54.575
and it is a real risk

00:08:54.575 --> 00:08:56.869
and we can't rest on belief.

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.829
We have to rest on reason.

00:08:58.829 --> 00:09:00.748
You know, belief is a dangerous path

00:09:00.748 --> 00:09:01.582
to being able

00:09:01.582 --> 00:09:02.875
to justify actions

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:03.918
on the basis of things

00:09:03.918 --> 00:09:05.586
that we can't interpret.

00:09:05.586 --> 00:09:07.171
At the same time,

00:09:07.171 --> 00:09:09.549
we are all behaviorists today.

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.551
We observe outputs.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:13.094
I don't really understand

00:09:13.094 --> 00:09:14.845
what's going on inside your mind.

00:09:14.845 --> 00:09:15.763
For example,

00:09:15.763 --> 00:09:17.682
I rely on the things that you say

00:09:17.682 --> 00:09:18.266
and the things

00:09:18.266 --> 00:09:19.350
that you do

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:22.812
to verify that you can repeatedly act

00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:23.813
consistently

00:09:23.813 --> 00:09:25.481
with your own behavior policy,

00:09:25.481 --> 00:09:27.024
your own set of values.

00:09:27.024 --> 00:09:29.026
And that's actually how we form

00:09:29.026 --> 00:09:31.028
trust in society today.

00:09:31.028 --> 00:09:32.029
We don't form trust

00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:33.489
by interrogating

00:09:33.489 --> 00:09:36.409
the precise causal explanation

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:38.077
of your own data patterns

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.496
based on your past personal history.

00:09:40.496 --> 00:09:42.081
Now, I'm not saying that we shouldn't

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:42.915
hold AIS

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.042
to even higher standards than ourselves,

00:09:45.042 --> 00:09:47.086
because clearly we're all in agreement

00:09:47.086 --> 00:09:48.254
that we don't want to be,

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:49.880
you know, disintermediated

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:50.673
from our position.

00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:51.340
As, you know,

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.842
top of the food chain in our

00:09:52.842 --> 00:09:55.386
in our species and in civilization today.

00:09:55.386 --> 00:09:56.679
But at the same time,

00:09:56.679 --> 00:09:57.763
we have to be realistic

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:58.556
about the benefits.

00:09:58.556 --> 00:10:00.433
Take health care, for example.

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:02.518
These models are performing

00:10:02.518 --> 00:10:04.353
an incredible role

00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:07.356
in being able to detect disease at, you

00:10:07.356 --> 00:10:08.399
know, human level

00:10:08.399 --> 00:10:11.485
performance across the board on radiology

00:10:11.485 --> 00:10:15.114
scans for chest x rays, for mammograms,

00:10:15.197 --> 00:10:16.574
for acute kidney injury,

00:10:16.574 --> 00:10:18.784
for sepsis, for glaucoma.

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:21.412
And you know, blinding eye diseases

00:10:21.412 --> 00:10:23.122
and the cost of producing

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:25.291
a world class diagnosis

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:26.500
and the proposed treatment

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.753
pathway is about to plummet

00:10:28.753 --> 00:10:30.546
to zero marginal cost.

00:10:30.546 --> 00:10:33.341
It is going to be essentially free

00:10:33.341 --> 00:10:34.717
in the next decade

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:35.384
to provide

00:10:35.384 --> 00:10:38.846
an absolutely world class diagnosis

00:10:38.888 --> 00:10:40.181
that's going to transform

00:10:40.181 --> 00:10:41.557
health care for billions

00:10:41.557 --> 00:10:42.642
and billions of people.

00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:43.267
And we're going to see

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:46.520
the same trajectory in education.

00:10:46.604 --> 00:10:47.855
We'll see the same trajectory

00:10:47.855 --> 00:10:49.440
in the development of food

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.067
and synthetic materials,

00:10:51.067 --> 00:10:52.652
and we'll see the same trajectory

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:53.235
for decision

00:10:53.235 --> 00:10:54.320
making and entrepreneurship

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.446
across the board.

00:10:55.446 --> 00:10:57.490
So the benefits are already incredible.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.699
The challenge is how can we

00:10:58.699 --> 00:10:59.992
mitigate those downsides?

